before:
With column direction the cross axis becomes horizontal here. One is centered left-to-right and Two sits at the right edge.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.row { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100px; width: 240px; align-items: center; } .row > div { width: 60px; height: 20px; } .two { align-self: flex-end; }
```

after:
This page uses ordinary left-to-right, horizontal text.

```css
.row {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
  width: 240px;
  height: 100px;
  align-items: center;
}
.row > div {
  width: 60px;
  height: 20px;
}
.two {
  align-self: flex-end;
}
```

The row runs horizontally, so its cross axis runs vertically.
